      "widgets_values": [
        "A single coherent cinematic 3D animated film frame, wide 16:9, from a camera in a FAMILY PICNIC GARDEN OUTSIDE a fenced dairy pasture. Morning light from upper left, 35mm natural perspective, child-eye camera height. Foreground garden: one child cushion on a woven mat at screen left, one low oak table with a sealed milk bottle in the center, one shaded wooden bench at screen right. Leave clear floor space for Alice kneeling left and Mother seated right. The family garden ends at a CLOSED FRONT PADDOCK FENCE running continuously from the LEFT EDGE to the RIGHT EDGE across the MIDDLE of the picture. A CLOSED wooden gate sits in this front fence. Its posts and rails are the nearest farm structures to camera, clearly BEHIND the garden furniture but IN FRONT of all cattle. A left return fence and right return fence connect to the front fence and recede into the distant pasture, making a real enclosed pen with unmistakable depth. Exactly TWO complete black-and-white adult dairy cows stand FAR BACK INSIDE that closed pen, about ten metres behind the front fence, small in the picture. Cow A stands side-on UNDER an open-sided timber milking shelter at back left; reserve an empty place beside her for an adult milkmaid, stool and pail later. Cow B grazes farther back at the right, visibly smaller than Cow A. Both cow heads, torsos, four legs and hooves stay wholly within the inner pasture; no part of either cow touches or crosses the front barrier. The front fence occludes the distant ground in front of them and is visually closer to camera. A small red barn and tree line recede softly behind the animals. Restrained sky, layered foreground foliage, believable object scale, consistent vanishing lines, grounded shadows and natural occlusion. This must read as a real three-dimensional film set, not a flat collage. No humans yet, no third cow, no cattle on the picnic side, no animal through the fence, no open gate, no indoor room, no typography, no logo and no watermark."
      ]
